(memory "llm/write" :when "the agent is about to have text written: one prompt sent to a model, or several messages as one conversation; or a write or converse call just failed or came back empty")
- (write "prompt") waits, gives reply string.

(write "Name three risks in this plan" :system "Be blunt." :max-tokens 200)
write-1: 84 words

- (converse messages) gives reply string, multi-turn. Message is
  (message :system "...") or (message :user "...") , alist with "role" and
  "content", so alist transcript is already valid. Bare string = user message.

(converse (list (message :system "Answer in one sentence.") (message :user q)))

Text arguments: prompt, :system, :instructions, extract text, message
content. Any value works: list or alist goes in printed. No (string …)
needed.

(memory "llm/extract" :when "the agent holds a text, page, comment or mail and must pull fields or structured data out of it, or an extract call just failed or returned the wrong shape")
(extract text shape) gives data shape describes, as Lisp data. Answer is
constrained to shape: no parsing, no prose to strip. Turns page, comment or
mail into fields read with assoc.

(extract page (shape (title "the page title")
    (stars :integer)
    (state (:enum "open" "closed"))
    (links (:list :string))
    (author (:optional (:string "who wrote it")))))
extract-1: alist, keys "title" "stars" "state" "links"

Shape is alist of (key . field) , written by (shape (name spec...) ...)
: no quote, no dotted pairs. Field is:
  :string, :number, :integer, :boolean, :any; plain string = string field
  described by its text;
  (:string "what it means") and same for other scalars;
  (:enum "a" "b") ; (:list field) ; (:optional field) , only field answer may
  omit; nested alist = nested object. Alist shape returns alist, (:list …)
  returns list. :instructions "..." says what to pull out.
  Nested group = nested object; (:list …) and (:optional …) take groups too:
(shape (items (:list (id :number) (title :string))))
  is list of objects. Shape is literal, built at compile time: computed enum
  needs hand-written alist.

(memory "llm/macros" :when "the agent holds a long text or many records that must be summarized, or a question must be answered from a given text or data, or answer just returned nil")
Three macros over write carry prompt for you; (doc 'summarize) and expansion
are all there is. Each takes write options plus :words, capping asked length
and token budget.

- (summarize value :words 60 [option...]) gives summary. Printed form goes in
  prompt, so list of records works like page of text.
- (summarize-each values :words 25 [option...]) gives summaries in order, one
  sequential call per element: slice with (head x 5) first, never hundreds.
- (answer question context :words 60 [option...]) answers from context
  only. nil: branch on it, do not echo it.

(setq brief (summarize acme/list-issues-1 :words 40))
brief: 39 words

(echo brief)

(setq owner (answer "who is assigned to ENG-12?" acme/list-issues-1))
owner: "Nadia"

(echo (if owner owner "the issues do not say who is assigned"))

(memory "llm/rewrites" :when "the agent must turn a text into a new one: swap its roles, say its opposite, blend two texts, take part out, add at the start or end, or state what follows from two statements")
Rewrites: new text from value. Any value works, printed. Each takes write
options, one call each:

- (invert x) swaps roles/direction: "I stand on giants." -> "Giants stand on me."
- (negate x) says opposite: "I am happy." -> "I am not happy."
- (blend x y) blends both into one text. (strip x y) takes y out of x:
  (blend (strip "Hello my enemy" "enemy") "friend") -> "Hello my friend".
- (open-with x y) works y in at start of x , (close-with x y) at end.
- (conclude x y) states what follows from both. (either x y) states as
  alternatives. (one-of x y) states exactly one holds.

(memory "llm/options" :when "a writing call needs a length cap, a temperature, a system line or a timeout, defaults must change for many calls, or a writing call just timed out")
Options, all optional, every call: :system · :max-tokens · :temperature ·
:reasoning-effort, :low, :medium or :high · :timeout ms, default 60000.
Timed-out call raises.

Global *writing-defaults* = keyword list every call starts from; call-site
option wins. (with-writing (option...) body...) extends it for one block,
restores after:

(with-writing (:max-tokens 120)
  (summarize-each (head pages-1 3)))
